WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.160
The screenwriter of M3GAN has said&nbsp;
her original screenplay was "way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.460
gorier" than the final cut of&nbsp;
the film. So can viewers ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.260
expect to see that blood-soaked unrated&nbsp;
version? The answer may surprise you.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.000
The new year in film has officially kicked&nbsp;
off with the campy horror thriller M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.580
from Universal Pictures and Blumhouse Productions.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.860
The stylish doll who lends the movie her name&nbsp;
became an internet icon ahead of the movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:32.520
January 2023 release thanks to the glee with which&nbsp;
she kills, as showcased in its first trailer.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.580
This preview particularly intrigued fans with a&nbsp;
scene in which M3GAN sashays with a handcrafted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.140
machete toward her next victim, building&nbsp;
anticipation for the horror comedy early on.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.260
The full movie lived up to the hype by leaning&nbsp;
into its campiness, earning an impressive 94%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:54.360
score on Rotten Tomatoes. This suggests&nbsp;
an extremely promising start as the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.420
premieres to enthusiastic theatergoers looking for&nbsp;
a bloody good time. M3GAN is notably produced by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:06.120
genre veteran James Wan, whose recent work has&nbsp;
helped usher in a new generation of horror.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.020
"I get accused of being the&nbsp;
master of killer doll movies."

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.180
Wan is credited with the story of M3GAN alongside&nbsp;
Akela Cooper, who serves as its principal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:20.220
screenwriter. The duo previously collaborated on&nbsp;
the mind-boggling action horror flick Malignant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.620
and are teaming up again for upcoming sequel&nbsp;
project The Nun 2. As it turns out, M3GAN in its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:31.020
final form is decidedly less bloody than in its&nbsp;
initial screenplay, which Cooper revealed might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:37.380
manifest as in unrated cut viewers will hopefully&nbsp;
see released before a possible M3GAN sequel.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.940
The final trailer for M3GAN gave viewers&nbsp;
a terrifying look at its titular doll's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:46.980
proficiency for killing and the deadly tactics&nbsp;
she employs against a few unfortunate victims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.900
who threaten either her or her best friend&nbsp;
Cady. In an interview published just before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.520
the film's release, writer Akela Cooper told&nbsp;
The L.A. Times that an unrated cut of M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.400
may already be in the works, featuring even more&nbsp;
violence. Cooper said of the film's screenplay:

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:23.520
Cooper also revealed that James Wan's input spared&nbsp;
several lives, as he credited her with writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.440
compelling characters undeserving of their deaths&nbsp;
as initially planned. Cooper told The L.A. Times:

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.740
The acclaimed writer also explained why&nbsp;
the movie was eventually toned down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.060
adhere to an intended PG-13 rating&nbsp;
— once M3GAN's dance went viral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.980
the teenage audience it developed online became&nbsp;
central to its marketing campaign. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.380
Cooper's interview hints that we may possibly see&nbsp;
a bloodier, unrated cut released in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:57.180
preserving M3GAN's rampage as initially&nbsp;
conceived for future fans of the film.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.380
In an interview GamesRadar published&nbsp;
just prior to the January 6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.400
2023 premiere of M3GAN, director&nbsp;
Gerard Johnstone explained that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.820
following a precedent set by Sam&nbsp;
Raimi horror comedy Drag Me To Hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:14.400
he decided to re-shoot certain scenes in order to&nbsp;
secure a PG-13 rating. Johnstone told the outlet:

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.560
While Johnstone may be a firm believer in&nbsp;
M3GAN as a PG-13 film, plenty of fans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.880
nevertheless interested in the possible unrated&nbsp;
cut that Akela Cooper floated. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.680
in a Reddit thread about Cooper's comments, one&nbsp;
user proposed that one particular scene would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.640
have benefitted from a higher gore quotient.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, another person wrote on Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.440
that they want to see a more detailed version of&nbsp;
a certain character's death in an unrated release.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:55.260
While Cooper may have mentioned the prospect of&nbsp;
an unrated M3GAN, there's not yet any official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.260 --> 00:04:00.660
word from either Universal or Blumhouse.&nbsp;
Of course, if fan interest remains high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.220
this bloodier version of M3GAN could&nbsp;
very well see the light of day.

